* $ is the number of the line the typewriter is on, from 1 to 54.
* Here it numbers the lines, and puts a blank line after every fifth.
1.1 Type $, x, x*2 in form 1.
1.2 Line if fp(x/5) = 0.
Form 1:
line __:   __ squared is ___
Do part 1 for x = 1(1)10.
line 14:    1 squared is   1
line 15:    2 squared is   4
line 16:    3 squared is   9
line 17:    4 squared is  16
line 18:    5 squared is  25

line 20:    6 squared is  36
line 21:    7 squared is  49
line 22:    8 squared is  64
line 23:    9 squared is  81
line 24:   10 squared is 100

